{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787713807286459001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"cybernetic-ferric-stallion","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":4,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"c43f299b67afdb9e2103aef74a2d49e2e3b23c314b7736d42e70d0244a002c98","event_uuid":"944ec549-29eb-43b5-a82c-c5c30d6bd2ea","position":{"commit_sha":"a9f811bad45889b09d11885c005990f1fc3f1962","position":"1787703100195364001-944ec549-29eb-43b5-a82c-c5c30d6bd2ea"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"4968b85d88a2df6848a89935c6c7ec0d92107839f15c069b3f3ec3cf4a157a69","event_uuid":"8c80915b-b8e0-4568-b4a0-4354ad601e3c","position":{"commit_sha":"da4149350a4718cc32bd2c7e57278416dcbc1159","position":"1787703116080390001-8c80915b-b8e0-4568-b4a0-4354ad601e3c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"9913f7b9a1aec603144a0fec1e087a3303b93fcda917b1ae4b83b8d30d66bb96","event_uuid":"23895e09-943f-440c-9ca7-e5921c4d0e65","position":{"commit_sha":"08d876bd7fbd9c2dd402e054c709a1ed2035d715","position":"1787703131941960001-23895e09-943f-440c-9ca7-e5921c4d0e65"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"8cc4e6415684d2e4a0b87ee2a32bf9ec90fcf45e786764260c23ce97fb8475e1","event_uuid":"12a66187-4ec0-4d61-9d42-706f661f848e","position":{"commit_sha":"259ae6ccc7f362ca47a21ac31cffa47d9162b179","position":"1787703202022564001-12a66187-4ec0-4d61-9d42-706f661f848e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787703100195364001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"23895e09-943f-440c-9ca7-e5921c4d0e65","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"3fa7-94ba-42aa-4623"},{"link_uuid":"12a66187-4ec0-4d61-9d42-706f661f848e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"81fd-c98b-9ca2-4a73"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nBug `soppy-logophilic-husky` (3fa7-94ba-42aa-4623) showed CI can LOSE test results without\nsaying so. Two properties, both outliving that specific budget:\n\n1. **Crashed workers silently drop tests.** Failing runs reported 16175 outcomes where the\n   passing parent reported 16182; locally the gap was ~95 vs 183. The suite ran more tests\n   than it reported, so a genuine failure inside a dropped test would have gone unseen.\n2. **The event was misattributed.** A red build on `main` was investigated as a defect in the\n   change under review (Gerrit 2098) because nothing named the real cause. `worker crashed` /\n   `node down: Not properly terminated` is runner infrastructure failing, not a test verdict.\n\nThis is a known ecosystem edge, not a local quirk: `pytest-timeout#137` documents the\ntimeout-plus-xdist worker crash exactly; `pytest-xdist#466`/`#932` document lost coverage and\ndouble-reported tests after a node dies.\n\n**How mature OSS projects handle it.** LLVM `lit` makes \"produced no result\" a first-class\noutcome — `UNRESOLVED`/`TIMEOUT` count as FAILURES, so the gap cannot exist. Jest fixed it in\nthe worker pool (`jest#13566`) after OOM-killed workers hung the run. For an OOM the framework\nis already dead, so the signal is read from outside: exit 137 = SIGKILL, 139 = SIGSEGV. None of\nthese projects ask contributors to hand-maintain expected test counts.\n\n## Scope boundary — CI matrix work is OWNED ELSEWHERE\nA parallel session currently owns CI performance, the Python-version matrix and 3.14 adoption,\nunder an approved pattern (oldest/newest supported in the Gerrit Verified gate; intermediate\nversions on the scheduled main sweep; macOS on the hot path but scoped to compatibility tests\nwhile Ubuntu runs the full suite; Windows considered for the scheduled sweep). **This story\nchanges no matrix, no lane, and no runner count.** It is deliberately confined to detection\nthat is in-process and therefore free of CI latency. The wider OSS-alignment backlog — endpoint\nPython versions, Windows, pre-merge CodeQL, widening Zizmor beyond `release.yml`, SHA-pinning\nactions, `twine check` in the artifact probe, external link checking, dependency-bound sweeps,\ndiff coverage — is recorded separately for that owner and is OUT OF SCOPE here.\n\n## Approach\nAdopt the runner-level pattern; do not invent bespoke accounting.\n\n**Rejected: reconciling outcome counts.** `pytest-xdist#932` shows crashed items are\nrescheduled and can report twice, so the arithmetic can overcount as well as undercount, and\nit would need hand-tuning for `-x`, `--maxfail` and `-k`/`-m` deselection. That is a\nchange-detector wearing an invariant's clothing.\n\n**Primary — in-process, CI-agnostic, zero added latency.** A new plugin module implements\n`pytest_testnodedown(node, error)` (xdist `newhooks.py:84`; xdist 3.8.0 is pinned here) and\nrecords every abnormal exit — `error` is non-`None` when a node dies rather than finishing. At\n`pytest_sessionfinish` it writes a red diagnostic naming the node id and the error, then\nescalates `session.exitstatus` to `pytest.ExitCode.TESTS_FAILED`.\n\nThat escalation is an ESTABLISHED SEAM here, not a novelty: `tests/conftest.py:718-735` already\ndoes exactly this for a leaked working tree, including the\n`terminalreporter.write_line(..., red=True)` diagnostic and the `session.exitstatus`\nassignment. This follows it. The plugin lives in its OWN module because `tests/conftest.py` is\n735 lines against the 800 cap in `.github/module-size-limit.txt`; conftest only registers it.\n\n**Secondary — the signal no in-process hook can see.** An OOM kill destroys the interpreter, so\n`pytest` cannot report it. A small `scripts/` helper maps a process exit status to a named\ncause (137 SIGKILL/likely-OOM, 139 SIGSEGV, 124 timeout) and prints a human-readable line. The\nLOGIC lives in `scripts/` where it is unit-testable and runnable by hand; the workflow touch is\na single call, keeping the collision surface with the CI owner to one line.\n\n**Portability.** Detection is in-process: it fires under `make test` on a laptop, under any CI\nprovider, and with no CI at all. The exit-status helper is a plain script, not a\nGitHub-Actions-only capability. Nothing here is triggered solely by one CI system.\n\n## Testing\nDrive a REAL crash, not a mock: a generated test calling `os._exit(1)` mid-run, in a child\npytest launched through `tests/_nested_pytest.py::run_nested_pytest` — the single sanctioned\nnested-launch site (story `phantasmal-enhanced-barnowl`) — under `-n 2`. Assert on the child's\nreturncode and output so the oracle exercises the real hook rather than a stub.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A crashed worker fails the run and names itself: a nested run whose test calls\n      `os._exit(1)` under `-n 2` exits non-zero and its output carries the worker id and the\n      node error; checked by `pytest tests/unit/test_crash_guard.py -k names_the_dead_worker`.\n- [ ] A crash cannot be masked by green tests — the same nested run with every OTHER test\n      passing still exits non-zero; checked by `-k not_masked_by_passing_tests`. This is the\n      property that failed in the incident: 16175 green outcomes beside 7 vanished ones.\n- [ ] The verdict comes from the HOOK, not from scraping output:\n      `grep -c \"node down\\|worker crashed\" tests/_crash_guard.py` returns 0, and the module\n      references `pytest_testnodedown`; checked by that grep plus the guard test.\n- [ ] Single-process runs are untouched: a nested run WITHOUT `-n` over a passing test exits 0\n      and prints no crash diagnostic; checked by `-k single_process_is_untouched`.\n- [ ] The exit-status helper names 137, 139 and 124 with distinct human-readable causes and\n      exits 0 for status 0; checked by `pytest tests/scripts/test_classify_runner_exit.py -q`,\n      which invokes it directly with no CI involved.\n- [ ] `tests/conftest.py` stays under the module-size cap: `wc -l < tests/conftest.py` is below\n      the value in `.github/module-size-limit.txt`; checked by the module-size CI gate.\n- [ ] No matrix, lane or runner-count change: `git diff origin/main -- .github/workflows/` adds\n      at most one invocation line plus comments, and changes no `python-version`, `os:` or\n      `matrix:` key; checked by reading that diff.\n- [ ] No regression: `make lint` and `make typecheck` exit 0, and\n      `pytest tests/unit/test_timeout_budget.py tests/unit/test_timeout_budget_headroom.py -q`\n      passes unedited.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/_crash_guard.py","reason":"new: pytest_testnodedown recorder + sessionfinish escalation"},{"path":"tests/conftest.py","reason":"register the plugin; must stay under the 800-line cap (currently 735)"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_crash_guard.py","reason":"new: real crash driven through run_nested_pytest under -n 2"},{"path":"scripts/classify_runner_exit.py","reason":"new: map 137/139/124 to named causes; logic lives here so it is unit-testable and hand-runnable"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_classify_runner_exit.py","reason":"new: exercises the helper directly, no CI involved"},{"path":".github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml","reason":"ONE invocation line for the exit-status helper; no matrix/lane/runner change (CI matrix is owned by a parallel session)"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["relates_to","81fd-c98b-9ca2-4a73"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"bab8-eb45-4dc2-4f02","ticket_type":"story","title":"Fail loudly when the runner eats test results","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["944ec549-29eb-43b5-a82c-c5c30d6bd2ea","8c80915b-b8e0-4568-b4a0-4354ad601e3c","23895e09-943f-440c-9ca7-e5921c4d0e65","12a66187-4ec0-4d61-9d42-706f661f848e"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787713807286459001,"uuid":"25c22642-56d2-4eba-b39c-e74543192fbf"}